    thinking: "**Defining the Expense Tracker**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on defining the core features. The plan is to create a web app expense tracker that\'s both comprehensive and high-quality, exactly as outlined. Right now, I\'m diving into the specifics of expense tracking: adding, editing, and deleting expenses with all their attributes (amount, title, category, tags, payment method, recurring status, etc.).\n\n\n**Expanding the Core Features**\n\nI\'ve been expanding the scope of core features. I am now working on a tagging system for expenses, alongside the core add/edit/delete functions. Additionally, I\'m fleshing out a recurring expense and income engine. It should handle auto-application across months, simplifying things for users.\n\n\n**Developing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dashboard\'s visualization tools. I\'m adding a daily spending trend with a line graph comparing actual spending against the prorated limit. I\'m also including category breakdowns via donut charts and a month-over-month income vs. expense comparison with bar charts. Reports and exports will also be part of the feature list.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 451911848
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
