  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on crafting a clean, modular architecture. I\'ve begun listing the core models and modules, and I\'m starting with `/src/types.ts`. The initial entry is the `Transaction` type, which currently includes `id`, `title`, `amount`, and `type`, specifying both expense and income.\n\n\n**Expanding Transaction Details**\n\nI\'ve significantly expanded the `Transaction` type to incorporate key details. This includes `category`, `date`, `tags`, optional `notes`, `paymentMethod`, optional `isRecurring` flag, and recurrence-related fields. I\'ve also defined the `Category` model with details like `id`, `name`, `icon`, `color`, and optional budget and daily prorated tracking. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined a `ProratedBudgetRule` model for managing budgets with options like custom item names, max monthly spend, the target month, and rollover configurations.\n\n\n**Adding Financial Instruments**\n\nI\'m now integrating financial instrument models. I\'ve defined `rollover` settings for prorated budgets. Also, I\'ve outlined `SavingsGoal` and `DebtItem` models. They include essential fields like IDs, amounts, dates, and historical records or payment details, for comprehensive financial tracking.\n\n\n**Defining Recurring Items**\n\nOkay, I\'m now outlining data structures to manage recurring financial events. I\'ve designed the `RecurringItem` model, detailing fields like frequency, application dates, and the `autoApply` flag for seamless integration. I\'ve also drafted models for budget alerts and user settings, setting the stage for smart notifications and a personalized financial experience.\n\n\n**Refining Alerts & Settings**\n\nI\'m currently focused on fine-tuning user settings. I\'ve defined `AlertThreshold`, `monthlyBudgetWarningThreshold`, and `enableRolloverByDefault`, along with `defaultMonth`. These settings will give the user control over budget alerts. Also, the `defaultMonth` allows for accurate tracking in the dashboard. I am also working on monthly, daily, and cumulative budgets based on user selections.\n\n\n**Implementing Visualizations & Exports**\n\nI\'m now integrating visualizations to offer spending insights. This includes daily spending bars compared to a ceiling line, a day-by-day table, and a calendar view with status badges for budget tracking. Alerts will highlight exceeded amounts, providing the exact delta. I\'ve also implemented CSV export functionality for all data, including transactions, monthly statements, and debt reports.\n\n\n**Adding Financial Analysis**\n\nI\'m now integrating financial analysis features, including amortization and interest calculations, and the payoff timeline and payment log. I have also added an engine for recurring transactions. This should streamline the budgeting process significantly. Furthermore, a rich tag system with multi-tagging on transactions and month-wise financial reports are being added. I\'m also organizing source code cleanly, and I\'ve started building seed data for immediate visualization, and utility formatters.\n\n\n**Developing Core Components**\n\nI\'ve outlined several key utilities and components. I\'ve developed budget calculation helpers for daily prorated calculations, budget status, and alert generation. My ExpenseContext is React Context with full local storage persistence, for state mutations. I\'ve designed a Navbar with month switching, notifications, and export options, and a SidebarNav for clean dashboard navigation and quick views.\n\n\n**Generating Visuals & Reports**\n\nI\'m now focusing on generating comprehensive month-wise financial reports and charts. I\'m building bar charts for cash flow analysis (income vs. expenses) and a pie chart for category distribution. I am also working on month-over-month comparisons, alongside CSV export options.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Modeling Recurring & Budgeting**\n\nMy next step is to get the structures around recurring transactions and budget management ironed out. I\'m focusing on defining monthly budgets at the category level, implementing rollover rules, and designing templates for recurring income and expenses with an auto-apply feature.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Tracking Savings and Debt**\n\nI am now focusing on modeling savings goals, incorporating progress tracking and deposit records. I will create a debt amortization and repayment tracker as well.\n\n\\n\\n\n**Configuring Categories & Alerts**\n\nI am now focusing on refining category and notification settings. I\'m adding options for custom category icons and colors. I am also planning push notification triggers based on user-defined alert thresholds.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 698768850
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
