  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Pinpointing Tab Render**\n\nOkay, I\'m trying to pinpoint where the tab switcher gets rendered. My initial thought was `App.tsx` or `Navbar.tsx`. I found that `App.tsx` handles `activeTab` and passes it to `Navbar`. I am currently re-investigating `Navbar.tsx`, just to be certain. I am now looking at the component\'s internal structure in detail.\n\n\n**Locating Tab Rendering**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining `Navbar.tsx`. I was wrong earlier, the tab bar isn\'t rendered there, even when checking lines 1-199! It receives `activeTab` and `onTabChange` from `App.tsx`, but no tab navigation is present. I\'m now thinking I need to create the tab navigation row itself, perhaps using a sleek design that aligns with the \"Immersive UI\" aesthetic. I need to make sure I match the design HTML requirements, including the deep atmospheric dark background and the glow background. I need to also implement the Dark Glass Cards design.\n\n\n**Defining UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the specific UI elements. I\'m taking notes on the required color palettes, including dark backgrounds (`bg-[#111114]`), glass borders, and blur effects for the tab bar and other elements. I\'ve broken down the style guidelines into specific components, with accents highlighted in electric lime. I\'m documenting text colors, including high-contrast options and alerts, alongside tag and input designs. I\'m also planning the dark modal\'s aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining UI Styles**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the specific styles. I am determining how to implement the vibrant glow effects with emerald/amber/cyan curves, considering elements like tooltip boxes and dark backgrounds. I\'m also examining typography choices, focusing on clean uppercase headers and high-contrast numerical displays. To ensure a complete style refresh, I\'m checking through all critical files in the codebase.\n\n\n"
