    thinking: "**Exploring Versatility**\n\nOkay, so I\'m really starting to see the power of `sql.js`. It\'s great that it can handle file persistence to a `.db` file in Node.js, AND that it can operate on the frontend, too! I\'m now thinking about how to build a full-stack Express server with persistent SQLite data using `sql.js` (and that `.db` file). My plan is to have real RESTful CRUD endpoints for transactions.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the API structure for the Express server. I\'ve got a detailed list of RESTful endpoints planned for transactions, categories, prorated budget rules, savings goals, debts, and recurring items, all designed for CRUD operations. I\'m imagining how each endpoint will interact with the SQLite database via sql.js, and mapping out the data flow for both reads and writes.\n\n\n"
