  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the full-stack SQLite integration, transitioning the expense tracker from browser local storage to a SQLite database with CRUD capabilities.\n\n### What Was Implemented\n\n- **SQLite Relational Persistence Layer**: Configured SQLite with table schemas (`transactions`, `categories`, `prorated_rules`, `savings_goals`, `debts`, `recurring_items`, `user_settings`, and `read_alerts`) persisted to `data/budget.sqlite`.\n- **RESTful Express API**: Implemented CRUD API endpoints in `server.ts` for all entities, supporting creation, batch imports, updates, deletions, debt installment schedules, savings contributions, and recurring bill generation.\n- **Client-Side API & State Synchronization**: Built `src/api/client.ts` and refactored `ExpenseContext.tsx` to automatically load data from SQLite upon initialization, persist all CRUD operations directly to the backend database, and synchronize live updates.\n- **SQLite Database Manager**: Added a database management modal in the navigation bar showing real-time connectivity status, disk storage stats, exact table row counts, on-demand re-syncing, and database re-seeding capabilities."
