  planner_response {
    response: "I have configured the application with Indian Rupee (**INR / \342\202\271**) as the default currency and verified the end-to-end user flows across all modules:\n\n### Key Enhancements & Verified User Flows\n\n- **Default Currency Configuration (\342\202\271 INR)**:\n  - Configured Indian Rupee (`\342\202\271` / `INR`) as the primary system currency across initial database seeding, user settings, and CSV statement generators.\n  - Updated the currency formatter to format numbers in the Indian locale (`en-IN`) when displaying `\342\202\271`.\n  - The currency dropdown in the header and the Settings view allows switching to other regional currencies (`$`, `\342\202\254`, `\302\243`, `\302\245`, `C$`, `A$`) dynamically.\n\n- **SQLite Database Architecture & Persistence**:\n  - Full CRUD operations are wired to the SQLite backend (`data/budget.sqlite`) for transactions, categories, prorated rules, savings goals, debt portfolios, recurring items, and alert acknowledgments.\n  - The **SQLite Manager** modal displays live table statistics, disk footprint, engine status, and a one-click database reseed action.\n\n- **Complete User Flow Verification**:\n  - **Dashboard**: Validated KPI calculations (Income, Expenses, Net Savings, Savings Rate), the prorated daily tracker spotlight for Snacks & Treats, spending pace trends, category distribution charts, and quick-action modals.\n  - **Prorated Limits**: Verified the daily budget calculation `(Monthly Budget + Rollover Surplus) / Days in Month`, day-by-day pacing indicators, overspend alerts, and rule creation/editing.\n  - **Transactions**: Verified instant filtering by category, type, and payment method, multi-field search, column sorting, pagination, and bulk CSV import/export.\n  - **Budgets & Recurring**: Tested monthly category caps, recurring item automation, and the **\"Apply Recurring for Month\"** batch transaction generator.\n  - **Savings & Debt**: Verified progress tracking, quick deposit logging with confetti celebrations, loan amortization tracking, and installment payment logging.\n  - **Reports & Export**: Verified monthly executive summaries, category utilization metrics, and CSV downloads."
    modified_response: "I have configured the application with Indian Rupee (**INR / \342\202\271**) as the default currency and verified the end-to-end user flows across all modules:\n\n### Key Enhancements & Verified User Flows\n\n- **Default Currency Configuration (\342\202\271 INR)**:\n  - Configured Indian Rupee (`\342\202\271` / `INR`) as the primary system currency across initial database seeding, user settings, and CSV statement generators.\n  - Updated the currency formatter to format numbers in the Indian locale (`en-IN`) when displaying `\342\202\271`.\n  - The currency dropdown in the header and the Settings view allows switching to other regional currencies (`$`, `\342\202\254`, `\302\243`, `\302\245`, `C$`, `A$`) dynamically.\n\n- **SQLite Database Architecture & Persistence**:\n  - Full CRUD operations are wired to the SQLite backend (`data/budget.sqlite`) for transactions, categories, prorated rules, savings goals, debt portfolios, recurring items, and alert acknowledgments.\n  - The **SQLite Manager** modal displays live table statistics, disk footprint, engine status, and a one-click database reseed action.\n\n- **Complete User Flow Verification**:\n  - **Dashboard**: Validated KPI calculations (Income, Expenses, Net Savings, Savings Rate), the prorated daily tracker spotlight for Snacks & Treats, spending pace trends, category distribution charts, and quick-action modals.\n  - **Prorated Limits**: Verified the daily budget calculation `(Monthly Budget + Rollover Surplus) / Days in Month`, day-by-day pacing indicators, overspend alerts, and rule creation/editing.\n  - **Transactions**: Verified instant filtering by category, type, and payment method, multi-field search, column sorting, pagination, and bulk CSV import/export.\n  - **Budgets & Recurring**: Tested monthly category caps, recurring item automation, and the **\"Apply Recurring for Month\"** batch transaction generator.\n  - **Savings & Debt**: Verified progress tracking, quick deposit logging with confetti celebrations, loan amortization tracking, and installment payment logging.\n  - **Reports & Export**: Verified monthly executive summaries, category utilization metrics, and CSV downloads."
