  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Code Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `src/` directory to pinpoint all the modules we need to document thoroughly. The key areas I\'m focusing on include the architecture, the prorated limits calculation engine along with its formulas, the categories and monthly budgets, and how transactions are managed, specifically considering filtering and the rest. I\'ll need to figure out the best way to present them.\n\n\n**Defining Documentation Scope**\n\nI\'ve scoped out the documentation needs. I\'m focusing on creating key documents: a comprehensive `README.md` for project overview and quickstart, an `ARCHITECTURE.md` detailing the full-stack design and state management, and a deep-dive into features in `FEATURES.md`, covering views and modal tools. I am thinking of a clear structure with diagrams to explain the system\'s function to an end user.\n\n\n**Expanding Documentation Outline**\n\nI\'m expanding the documentation outline, focusing now on more specific API documentation in `API_REFERENCE.md`. I also want a guide covering the math behind the prorated budgeting in `PRORATED_BUDGETING_GUIDE.md`, and a database schema description at `DATABASE_SCHEMA.md` to cover everything. I\'m keen on establishing the structure for this documentation right away.\n\n\n"
